# =============================================================================
# Site-monitor cadence watchdog cron (NFM-5309)
# =============================================================================
# Host-side detector for GitHub scheduled-event starvation. The GH scheduler
# chronically delivers ~8 events/day to site-monitor.yml regardless of the
# nominal cron (NFM-5226 root cause; NFM-5309 W40 census: 5.5% of */10
# nominal, ~9% of the 17 */6 watchdog nominal). Nothing inside GitHub
# Actions can detect that — a starved scheduler cannot be its own watchdog —
# so this check runs HERE, next to the NFM-5226 on-host sentinel.
#
# Script: scripts/site_monitor_cadence_check.py (pure logic unit-tested in
# scripts/tests/test_site_monitor_cadence_check.py; `gh` is the only dep).
#
# Exit-code semantics (cron mails / logs non-zero output):
#   0 OK (≥ warn-below runs delivered in window)
#   1 execution error (gh missing/failed — do NOT page as cadence)
#   2 WARN    — delivered < 4 runs / 24h (half the census baseline)
#   3 CRITICAL— zero runs / 24h OR newest run older than 18h (blackout)
#
# SRE §3 census reuse: the same script with --json emits the census record.
#
# =============================================================================
# INSTALLATION
# =============================================================================
# Copy WHOLE blocks — partial copies are dead-on-arrival (NFM-5309 CR F1):
#   - the PATH line is REQUIRED (cron's default /usr/bin:/bin has no
#     homebrew gh on Apple Silicon), and
#   - the definition lines must ride along with the schedule line, or every
#     variable expands empty and the detector never runs.
#
# macOS per-user crontab: extract the 5 marked lines and append to crontab —
#
#   awk '/^# >>>macos-per-user$/{f=1;next} /^# <<<macos-per-user$/{f=0} f' \
#     scripts/cron/site-monitor-cadence.cron | sed 's/^# //' \
#     > "$TMPDIR/cadence-cron"
#   (crontab -l 2>/dev/null; cat "$TMPDIR/cadence-cron") | crontab -
#
# or paste them by hand (verbatim, all 5, no `root` field):
#
# >>>macos-per-user
# PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
# REPO_DIR=/Users/lwj04/Projects/nucpot
# PYTHON=/opt/homebrew/bin/python3.14
# LOG_DIR=/Users/lwj04/Library/Logs/nucpot-site-monitor-cadence
# 41 */4 * * * mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && cd "$REPO_DIR" && "$PYTHON" scripts/site_monitor_cadence_check.py >> "$LOG_DIR/cadence.log" 2>&1
# <<<macos-per-user
#
# Uninstall: crontab -l | grep -v site_monitor_cadence_check | crontab -
# (launchd alternative: docs/runbooks/latched-error-recovery.md §5 pattern.)
#
# Linux (/etc/cron.d): install the whole file as-is (the `root` user field
# below is REQUIRED in /etc/cron.d and REJECTED by per-user crontabs — which
# is why the macOS block above omits it):
#
#   sudo install -m 0644 scripts/cron/site-monitor-cadence.cron \
#     /etc/cron.d/nucpot-site-monitor-cadence
#
# Verify after install under cron's environment (not your interactive shell):
#   env -i PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/bin:/bin HOME="$HOME" \
#     "$PYTHON" scripts/site_monitor_cadence_check.py --json
#   → expect rc=0 and delivered ≈ 6-10 under current starvation baseline.
# =============================================================================

PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
REPO_DIR=/Users/lwj04/Projects/nucpot
PYTHON=/opt/homebrew/bin/python3.14
LOG_DIR=/Users/lwj04/Library/Logs/nucpot-site-monitor-cadence

# Every 4h at :41 (off the start-of-hour drop window; 6 checks/day is ample
# for a 24h evaluation window). One invocation; every verdict line lands in
# cadence.log — SRE's heartbeat greps that log exactly like the NFM-5226
# sentinel log. (Do NOT add an `||` re-run: it would double-count gh calls
# and treat exit-1 execution errors as cadence alerts.)
41 */4 * * * root mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR" && cd "$REPO_DIR" && \
    "$PYTHON" scripts/site_monitor_cadence_check.py \
    >> "$LOG_DIR/cadence.log" 2>&1
